    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    ///   <para>&lt;http://purl.oclc.org/NET/ssnx/qu/dim#ThermalConductivity&gt;</para>
    ///   <para>Thermal conductivity is the constant k in the formula q = -k grad T where q is the heat transfer per unit time per unit area of a surface normal to the direction of transfer and grad T is the temperature gradient. Thermal conductivity is a property of the material.</para>
